        <headline>Special Weather Statement issued September 26 at 3:47PM AST by NWS San Juan PR</headline>
        <description>At 347 PM AST, Doppler radar was tracking a line of strong
thunderstorms extending westward from Corozal and Morovis to Utuado.
These storms are nearly stationary.

HAZARD...Wind gusts up to 50 mph. Funnel clouds and small size hail
are possible.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Minor damage to outdoor objects is possible. Gusty winds
could knock down tree limbs and blow around unsecured
objects.

Locations impacted include...
Jayuya, Ciales, Morovis, Orocovis, Utuado, Barahona, Franquez and
Cayuco.
</description>
        <instruction>If outdoors, consider seeking shelter inside a building.

Frequent cloud to ground lightning is occurring with this storm.
Lightning can strike 10 miles away from a thunderstorm. Seek a safe
shelter inside a building or vehicle.

Torrential rainfall is also occurring with these storms and may lead
to flash flooding. Do not drive your vehicle through flooded
roadways.</instruction>
